# Choice dialogues of the storyline payoff scenes (T-143). Compiled to zz_fs_storyline_scenes.json.

dialogue story.pie.talk
n0 marcus: One slice of my pie. Her door. No name. If she asks, a stranger with excellent taste.
  next n1
n1 marcus: Well? You can say no. I'll just stand here holding it.
  ? Deliver it, no tricks. => r0 | flag:choice.pie.honest
  ? I'll improve it on the way. => r1 | flag:choice.pie.improve
  ? It might not survive the walk. => r2 | flag:choice.pie.eat
r0 -: You leave the slice on Odalys's step. She reads the note, sighs, and takes a bite.
  next r0b
r0b odalys: A stranger with excellent taste and sawdust on the note. ...It's rather good. Tell him nothing.
  expr thinking
r1 -: You add a pinch of cinnamon on the way. Odalys tastes it, then frowns at it for a long time.
  next r1b
r1b odalys: Someone added cinnamon. It's better now. I resent that, professionally.
  expr embarrassed
r2 -: You eat the slice on the road. It is excellent. Two bakers will hear about this.
  next r2b
r2b odalys: An empty plate and a crumb on your sleeve. I'll bill Marcus for one pie. You, for the crumb.

dialogue story.notes.dorian
n0 -: A folded note sits half under the door. Dorian's hand is still on it.
  next n1
n1 dorian: ...So. Now you know who.
  ? Just smile at him. => r0 | flag:choice.notes.dorian.smile
  ? Thank him. => r1 | flag:choice.notes.dorian.thanks | friend:dorian,10
  ? Slip a note back under his door. => r2 | flag:choice.notes.dorian.note | friend:dorian,15
r0 dorian: ...A smile. No words. You speak my language.
  expr embarrassed
r1 dorian: You're welcome. I'll go be flustered behind a tree.
  expr happy
r2 dorian: For me? ...I'll read it in the forest. Twice.
  expr happy

dialogue story.notes.juno
n0 -: Juno has a folded note halfway under a door. She stops. So do you.
  next n1
n1 juno: ...So. Now you know. All of them were me. Mostly in pencil.
  ? Say nothing. Just smile. => r0 | flag:choice.notes.juno.smile
  ? Thank her for them. => r1 | flag:choice.notes.juno.thanks | friend:juno,10
  ? Write her one back. => r2 | flag:choice.notes.juno.note | friend:juno,15
r0 juno: ...You smiled. Okay. That's a lot of kindness for one face to hold.
  expr embarrassed
r1 juno: Oh. Oh no, that's the whole reward. I'm going to go be flustered behind the rain barrel.
  expr happy
r2 juno: A note? For me? ...I'm keeping it. In a drawer I'm inventing right now. Label pending.
  expr happy

dialogue story.notes.tilda
n0 -: Tilda slides a folded note under a door and straightens up. Neither of you moves.
  next n1
n1 tilda: ...Well. Now you know who's been doing it. Wren mustn't find out. She'd want a cut.
  ? Say nothing. Just smile. => r0 | flag:choice.notes.tilda.smile
  ? Thank her for the notes. => r1 | flag:choice.notes.tilda.thanks | friend:tilda,10
  ? Slip a note back. Unsigned, obviously. => r2 | flag:choice.notes.tilda.note | friend:tilda,15
r0 tilda: ...A smile. No chalk, no receipt. That's the hardest kind to put on a slate.
  expr embarrassed
r1 tilda: Don't thank me, I'd rather you owed me. ...Oh, now I'm flustered. I'll go rearrange something.
  expr happy
r2 tilda: A note, for me? ...I'm keeping it. In a drawer I've just invented.
  expr happy

dialogue story.umbrella.talk
n0 -: A large red umbrella hangs open on the fence post, dripping with great dignity. Piper points at it.
  next n1
n1 piper: Third time it's wandered off. It always turns up drier than I do. What do we do?
  ? Give it back to her. => r0 | flag:choice.umbrella.return
  ? Leave it on the fence. => r1 | flag:choice.umbrella.hang
  ? Keep it. It suits me. => r2 | flag:choice.umbrella.keep
r0 piper: Reunited! I'd write it a song, but it would wander off mid-verse.
  expr happy
r1 piper: Leave it? ...Yes. A little red landmark. Somebody out in this rain needs it more.
r2 piper: You're keeping it? That's theft with excellent manners. ...It does suit you.
  emote sweat

dialogue story.scarecrow.talk
n0 tilda: Mine is smiling. Crows can't stand a cheerful face. That's simply known.
  next n1
n1 dorian: Mine says nothing. Crows hate that. I watched them for a week.
  next n2
n2 tilda: Well? Whose scarecrow is guarding the fields this fall?
  ? Tilda's, obviously. => r0 | flag:choice.scarecrow.tilda
  ? Dorian's. Sorry, Tilda. => r1 | flag:choice.scarecrow.dorian
  ? It's a tie. => r2 | flag:choice.scarecrow.tie
  ? Let the crows decide. => r3 | flag:choice.scarecrow.crows
r0 tilda: Ha! Taste! Take the runner-up home. It'll stand in your field being thoughtful at the crows.
  expr happy
r1 dorian: ...Mine. Oh. Take the runner-up home. It doesn't talk either.
  expr happy
r2 tilda: A tie. Coward. Take one anyway, and we'll both be wounded together.
  emote sweat
r3 dorian: The crows. ...They sat on both. Equally. A tie, then. Take one.
  expr thinking

dialogue story.whistler.bram
n0 bram: I whistle. Don't tell Wren. She'd count the notes as words.
  next n1
n1 bram: ...Well?
  ? Wave and say a cheerful hello. => r0 | flag:choice.whistler.bram.hello
  ? Whistle the wrong note back. => r1 | flag:choice.whistler.bram.back | friend:bram,10
  ? Say nothing. Just listen. => r2 | flag:choice.whistler.bram.listen | friend:bram,10
r0 bram: Hm. Hello. Yes. We'll blame the wind. It owes me.
r1 bram: Hm? ...That's my wrong note. Twenty years. Nobody's ever caught it.
  expr embarrassed
r2 bram: ...Hm. You listened. All of it. Most people leave before the end.
  expr happy

dialogue story.whistler.marcus
n0 marcus: It's a family tune. My grandfather hit one note wrong, and we've all kept it since.
  next n1
n1 marcus: ...Well? Go on. Everybody has an opinion about the note.
  ? Say hello, like a normal neighbor. => r0 | flag:choice.whistler.marcus.hello
  ? Whistle the wrong note back. => r1 | flag:choice.whistler.marcus.back | friend:marcus,10
  ? Say nothing. Wait for the encore. => r2 | flag:choice.whistler.marcus.listen | friend:marcus,10
r0 marcus: Hello. Yes. Hello. A normal approach. It's rarer than you'd think.
r1 marcus: You got the wrong note exactly right. I'm moved. Also mortified.
  expr embarrassed
r2 marcus: You listened. All of it. ...Grandfather would have liked you. I may whistle again. Quietly.
  expr happy

dialogue story.whistler.felix
n0 felix: I only whistle when I'm happy. Lately that's most evenings. Couldn't tell you why. ...Well. I could.
  next n1
n1 felix: ...Well? Say something. The quiet's worse.
  ? Call out a friendly hello. => r0 | flag:choice.whistler.felix.hello
  ? Whistle the wrong note back. => r1 | flag:choice.whistler.felix.back | friend:felix,10
  ? Say nothing. Just listen. => r2 | flag:choice.whistler.felix.listen | friend:felix,10
r0 felix: Hello. Yes. Hello back. Very sensible, given the circumstances.
r1 felix: You got the wrong note exactly right. Nobody's ever whistled back. ...I've gone red. It's the sunset.
  expr embarrassed
r2 felix: You listened. The whole tune. Nobody's done that but the pond. ...I may whistle again. Quietly.
  expr happy
